

My-app running in a Pod which connect to Mysql DB pod for storage

once pod restart the data will be lost, 

Storage Requirements:
1) Storage that doesn't depend on the pod lifecycle.
2) storage must be AVAILABLE on all nodes just not specific one
3) Storage needs to survive even if cluster crashes


Persistent storage: pv 
- a cluster resource
- created via yaml file
- need actual physical storage
- nfs-server or local disk or cloud-storage
- external plugin to your cluster
- PV are not namespaced, they are availale to all in the cluster
- PV outside of namespace
//////
apiVersion: v1
kind: Persistentvolume
metadata:
    name: pv-name
spec:
    capacity:
        storage: 5Gi
    volumeMode: Filesystem
    accessModes:
        - ReadWriteOnce
    persistentVolumeReclaimPolicy: Recycle
    storageClassName: slow
    mountOptions:
        - hard
        - nfsvers=4.0
    nfs:
      path: /dir/path/on/nfs/server
      server: nfs-server-ip-address
      
    //////
Local Vs Remote Volume types:

Application has to claim the Persistent Volume
pvc - claim voulme storage 10Gi ReadWriteOnce

pvc are created using yaml configuration

////
apiVersion: v1
kind: PersistentVolumeClaim
metadata:
    name: pvc-name
spec:
    storageClassName: manual
    volumeMode: FileSystem
    accessModes:
        - ReadWriteOnce
    resources:
        requests:
            storage: 10Gi

////
apiVersion: v1
kind: Pod
metadata: 
    name: myPod
spec:
    containers:
      - name: myfrontend
        image: nginx
        volumeMounts:
        - mountPath: "/var/www/html"
          name: myPod
    volumes:
      - name: mypd
        persistentVolumeClaim:
          claimName: pvc-name
//////
Volume is mounted into the Pod
Volume is mounted into container
read/write 
Pod requests the volume through PV claim
Claim tries to find a volume in cluster
Volume has the actual storage backed
Claims must be in same namespace!

